+    # Building the proof runs its code (commands, macros, tactics) as this user. It builds in its
+    # own PID namespace and a private mount namespace where all of $HOME is read-only (the
+    # toolchain, elan's proxies, this checkout, the package's sources, lakefile and .lake but its
+    # build directory, the lake packages, the replay cache), with a private /tmp. The
+    # oleans of the statement's closure, lake's configuration cache, the toolchain, the driver and
+    # the cache are fingerprinted before and after it (in this process's memory), and no module of
+    # the package may take a toolchain root's name: any difference fails the run.
+    toolchain="$(cd "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$(lake env which lean)")")/.." && pwd)"
+    # The toolchain must be the one tools/certify/toolchain.sha256 records (a digest of every
+    # file's SHA-256), so that nothing an earlier run executed has changed it.
